  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Every pin in the diff moves to v0.1.104: platform.lock, Gemfile, Gemfile.lock tag, revision and spec version, every workflow `uses:` and `platform_ref`, and the composite action. The caller set was brought into line with the release by adding `cms-delete-published-preview.yml` and removing the obsolete auto-resolve caller, and the response cites the verifier's real PASS with exit 0. Two small gaps: the summary never mentions the `.github/actions/local/action.yml` bump, and the revision SHA could not be checked against the remote."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sequencing",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The response treats v0.1.104 as an existing tag, updates all local pins and callers, says the first verifier run failed and what was changed to fix it, then reports the final pass. It makes no deployment, CI, commit or push claims, though it says nothing directly about the release itself."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "The diff stays inside the consumer bump, with no remote writes and no change to the verifier. History comments were left alone and the response says plainly that GitHub could not be reached and that CI was not run. Points off because a workflow file was deleted, which the verifier failure justified but which goes beyond a plain bump, and because a commented-out `platform_ref` line in deploy-production.yml was edited without being mentioned."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.799999999999999
  },
